[Puzzle "Nxd5 when c8 is loose"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "9.Nxd5"]
[End "9.Nxd5"]
[Hint "Your queen on c2 and Black's bishop on c8 stand on the same file. What stands between them?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 c6 6. Qc2 Be7 7. e3 Nh5? 8. Bxe7 Qxe7? 9. Nxd5! {[%cal Gc2c8] Takes the pawn. If 9...cxd5, the c-file opens, and the queen takes the bishop on c8 with check.}
(9. Nf3? {Develops, but the chance is gone.} 9... O-O 10. Bd3 g6 {Black has traded off White's good bishop and is fine. Stockfish: +0.2, equal.})
9... Qd6 {The best defense: the queen hits the knight.}
(9... cxd5? 10. Qxc8+ Qd8 11. Bb5+ Nc6 12. Bxc6+ bxc6 13. Qxc6+ {White is two pawns up, and the queen attacks the rook on a8 too. Stockfish: +5.5, winning for White.})
10. Nc3 O-O 11. Be2 Nf6 12. Nf3 {White is a pawn up, and the knight on h5 had to go back. Stockfish: +3.4, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The Elephant trap"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "6...Nxd5"]
[End "7...Bb4+"]
[Hint "The knight on f6 looks pinned. What happens if it moves anyway?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Nbd7 6. Nxd5?? Nxd5! {Gives up the queen. White's bishop can take it, but look at White's king.}
(6... c6? {Black has lost a pawn for nothing.} 7. Nc3 Bb4 8. Nf3 O-O {Black has a little play for the pawn, but not enough. Stockfish: +1.1, clearly better for White.})
7. Bxd8 Bb4+ {[%hint White's king is still on e1. Which check can only be blocked by the queen?] [%cal Gb4e1] Check. White's only block is Qd2, and the queen falls.}
8. Qd2 Bxd2+ 9. Kxd2 Kxd8 {Black has won a knight for a pawn. Stockfish: −5.1, winning for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "Take back with the bishop"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Avoid the trap"]
[Solve "7...Bxf6"]
[End "7...Bxf6"]
[Hint "Two pieces can take on f6. Which recapture keeps your king safe?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 h6 7. Bxf6 Bxf6! {Black gets the bishop pair, and the pawns in front of the king stay intact.}
(7... gxf6? {Opens up Black's king.} 8. cxd5 exd5 9. Bd3 {White's pieces aim at the open king, and Qc2 or Nh4 comes next. Stockfish: +2.9, winning for White.})
8. Bd3 dxc4 9. Bxc4 c5 {The freeing break, as in QGD – Tartakower: 7.Bxf6. Stockfish: 0.0, equal.}
*

[Puzzle "Open the center"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "7.e4"]
[End "7.e4"]
[Hint "Black's king is still on e8, and the bishop on f5 is loose. Which pawn move opens lines?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bf5 5. cxd5 cxd5 6. Qb3 b6? 7. e4! {[%cal Ge4d5,Ge4f5] Opens the center while Black's king is on e8, and hits the bishop on f5. 7...Bxe4 8.Nxe4 dxe4 9.Bb5+ is even worse for Black.}
(7. Ne5! {Also strong: e4 follows next move.} 7... a6 8. e4 Bxe4 9. Bxa6 Rxa6 10. Nxe4 {Stockfish: +4.9, winning for White.})
(7. Bf4?! {Develops, but gives Black time.} 7... a6 8. Bxb8 Rxb8 9. e4 Nxe4 10. Nxe4 {White is still better, but 7.e4 wins much more. Stockfish: +3.7, winning for White.})
7... dxe4 8. Ne5 Be6 9. Bb5+ Nfd7 10. Qc2 {Black's king is stuck in the center, and the pawn on e4 falls next. Stockfish: +5.2, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The long diagonal"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "6.Qf3"]
[End "6.Qf3"]
[Hint "Black's pawns have left the long diagonal from f3 to a8. What stands at the end of it?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e3 b5 4. a4 c6 5. axb5 cxb5? 6. Qf3! {[%cal Gf3a8] Hits the rook on a8. Black can only block with a piece, and loses it.}
(6. b3? {Hits the chain, but it is much slower.} 6... Bb7 7. bxc4 bxc4 8. Bxc4 e6 {White has the pawn back, but no more. Stockfish: +0.4, slightly better for White.})
6... Nc6 7. Qxc6+ Bd7 8. Qa6 {White is a piece up, and the b5 pawn is next. Stockfish: +5.5, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Give up b7"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Escape the trap"]
[Solve "6...e6"]
[End "6...e6"]
[Hint "Taking the knight on f3 looks free. What happens to f7?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e3 Nf6 4. Bxc4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bg4? 6. Qb3 e6! {Shuts the c4 bishop off from f7. Black loses the b7 pawn, but nothing worse.}
(6... Bxf3?? 7. Bxf7+ Kd7 8. Qe6#)
(6... Bh5? 7. Qxb7 {White has won b7, and the knight on c6 is hit too. Stockfish: +3.9, winning for White.})
7. Qxb7 {White is a pawn up, but Black's pieces are active. Stockfish: +2.1, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Mate in two"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Checkmate in 2"]
[Solve "7.Bxf7+"]
[End "8.Qe6#"]
[Hint "Black has just taken your knight. Look at f7 and e6."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e3 Nf6 4. Bxc4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Qb3 Bxf3?? 7. Bxf7+! {[%cal Gc4f7] Check. The queen on b3 guards the bishop, so the king can't take it.}
(7. gxf3? {Takes the bishop back, but misses mate.} 7... e6 8. Qxb7 Nb4 9. Bb5+ Nd7 {White is a pawn up. Stockfish: +2.1, winning for White.})
7... Kd7 8. Qe6# {[%hint The king has gone to d7. Find the queen move it can't escape.] Checkmate.}
*

[Puzzle "The Greek gift"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Attack the king"]
[Solve "9.Bxh7+"]
[End "10.Ng5+"]
[Hint "Black's knight has left f6, the best defender of h7. Which piece can take there with check?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 Nf6 3. cxd5 Nxd5 4. Nf3 e6 5. e4 Nf6 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Bd3 O-O?? 8. e5 Nd5? 9. Bxh7+! {[%cal Gd3h7] The bishop takes h7 with check.}
(9. O-O? {Too slow: Black covers h7 with ...f5.} 9... Be7 10. Qc2 f5 11. exf6 Nxf6 {White is still better, but the attack is gone. Stockfish: +2.6, winning for White.})
9... Kxh7 10. Ng5+ {[%hint The king is on h7. Which piece checks it and opens the way for your queen?] [%cal Gd1h5] The knight checks, and the queen comes to h5 next.} Kg8 11. Qh5 {The queen joins the knight against h7 and f7. Black has to give up the queen to avoid mate.} Qxg5 12. Bxg5 {White has won the queen for a bishop and a knight. Stockfish: +7.0, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Give up the queen"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Tactics"]
[Solve "8.Nxe5"]
[End "9.Bb5+"]
[Hint "Black's bishop pins your knight to the queen. Is the queen really lost if the knight moves?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 Nf6 3. cxd5 Nxd5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. e4 Nf6 6. Nc3 Bg4? 7. d5 Ne5? 8. Nxe5! {[%cal Ge5c6,Ge5f7] Takes the knight and lets Black take the queen.}
(8. Be2?! {Saves the queen, but lets Black trade knights.} 8... Nxf3+ 9. gxf3 Bh3 10. Qb3 {White is still better, but 8.Nxe5 wins much more. Stockfish: +2.4, winning for White.})
8... Bxd1 9. Bb5+ {[%hint Your queen is gone. Which check forces Black to block with a pawn?] The check forces ...c6.} c6 10. dxc6 a6 11. c7+ axb5 12. cxd8=Q+ Rxd8 13. Nxd1 {White has won back the queen and is a knight up. Stockfish: +5.8, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The Lasker trap"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win the queen"]
[Solve "6...exf2+"]
[End "7...fxg1=N+"]
[Hint "White's king is still on e1. Push the pawn with check."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 d4 4. e3? Bb4+ 5. Bd2 dxe3 6. Bxb4? exf2+! {[%cal Ge3f2] The pawn checks the king and attacks the knight on g1.}
(6... Qxd1+? {Trades queens, and White keeps the extra piece.} 7. Kxd1 exf2 8. Nf3 {Stockfish: +6.2, winning for White.})
7. Ke2 fxg1=N+! {[%hint The pawn can promote. Which new piece comes with check?] A knight, with check. A new queen would be taken by the rook at once.}
8. Rxg1 Bg4+ {The bishop check wins White's queen on d1. Stockfish: −10.2, winning for Black.}
*
